  "note": "Municipal elections, 21 May 1958. Contests in Town Hall Ward (recorded) and Market Ward (result not yet found). In Harryville Ward the alderman, J. S. M'Ilhagga, and the four councillors were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1958, p. 6). All four elected were retiring members. Other wards were unopposed and are not named in this report."
